            <ArticleTitle>An 18-Year-Old Woman Who Was Found Down.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1124-1125</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0002-9149(16)32022-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.amjcard.2016.11.068</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 18-year-old woman was found unresponsive by her mother. After the patient spontaneously regained consciousness, an electrocardiogram showed a markedly prolonged QT interval thought to be due to congenital long QT1. An implantable cardioverter defibrillator was placed. After being free of symptoms for 1 year, she spontaneously developed torsades de pointes that was successfully terminated by the defibrillator.</AbstractText>
